Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; =====================================================================
; H.E.D.Z. - registry reference (CORRECTED)
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; WHY THIS FILE LOOKS THE WAY IT DOES
;
;   * Hedz.exe is a 32-BIT program, so it reads the 32-BIT registry view:
;         HKLM\SOFTWARE\WOW6432Node\Vis Interactive\Hedz
;     A .reg file imported with a 64-bit reg.exe writes the 64-bit view
;     (HKLM\SOFTWARE\Vis Interactive\Hedz) where the game never looks.
;     That mistake produced a permanent "insert the CD" prompt.
;     For this reason the key path below is written EXPLICITLY as
;     WOW6432Node. Alternative:  reg.exe import /reg:32 hedz-install.reg
;
;   * The value names are the ones the ORIGINAL installer script writes.
;     Evidence: D:\ENGLISH\SETUP.INS contains
;         Software\Vis Interactive\Hedz
;         Language
;         InstalledFromDrive
;         InstallType
;
;   * InstalledFromDrive MUST INCLUDE THE COLON -- store "D:", never "D".
;     Hedz.exe concatenates the value verbatim:
;         RegQueryValueExA(...,"InstalledFromDrive",...)
;         strcpy(base, value); strcat(base, "\\Hedz\\");
;         driveLetter = base[0];
;     No colon is inserted anywhere. A bare "D" therefore builds the RELATIVE
;     path "D\Hedz\...", which resolves against the game's own folder instead
;     of the CD. A Process Monitor trace of the real game showed exactly that:
;         CreateFile C:\Games\HEDZ\D\Hedz\test        -> PATH NOT FOUND
;         CreateFile C:\Games\HEDZ\D\Hedz\Music\1.MUS -> PATH NOT FOUND
;     With "D:" the same trace shows D:\Hedz\test -> ACCESS DENIED (correct,
;     the CD is write-protected) and D:\Hedz\Music\1.mus..7.mus -> SUCCESS.
;
;   * Without InstalledFromDrive the game reports
;     "Registry Entry Not found, full protection" and demands the CD.
;
; Prefer tools\Set-HedzCdPath.ps1 (writes both views, validates the disc).
; =====================================================================

; ---- the values the game reads (32-bit view) ----
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\WOW6432Node\Vis Interactive\Hedz]
"InstalledFromDrive"="D:"
"Language"="English"
; "InstallType"="..."      ; only if the CD prompt persists; value unknown,
;                          ; try 1 / Full - see README Task 2

; ---- uninstall bookkeeping (32-bit view, so 32-bit Add/Remove sees it) ----
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\WOW6432Node\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Uninstall\{5BAA97BC-718C-11D2-84B1-006097616E32}]
"DisplayName"="HEDZ"
"InstallLocation"="C:\\GAMES\\HEDZ"
"DisplayVersion"="1.0"
"Publisher"="VIS Interactive / Hasbro Interactive"

; NOTE: there is deliberately no UNINST.EXE entry - the CD's installer
; generates that file at install time and a manual install does not have it.
; Uninstalling = delete the game folder and the two keys above.
